# The original threefold's delta-circle sweep

The period-one circle acts by the original vertical translations on the
original glued threefold. Its actual positive-circle singular cross
product defines the sweep. The proved vanishing of native first homology
makes this degree-one sweep zero.

On the unchanged marked regular fibres it is the genuine delta-first
Pontryagin product, with ordered coordinates `(0,0,-v₀,0,-v₁,-v₂)`.
The regular coinvariant therefore gives the actual relation `-6v₀` and
annihilation of global second homology by six, not a primitive unit claim.

On the original central elliptic surfaces, the original finite covers
intertwine the same action. Actual transfer and the unchanged Wang
markings determine the sweep matrix, prove divisibility of the genuine
covering shear, and produce native global-kernel classes with unit second
coordinate. No duality, replacement space, or chosen-basis identification
is assumed.
-/
